 "command": "python -m oculstorm.realtime_inputs",
 "reading": [
  "A measurement, not a candidate: no model or default changes, so there is nothing to promote and the label is no-gain.",
  "With real-time ACE inputs delayed 1 hour, validation MSE over all hours is 22.5% higher for XGBoost and 28.4% higher for the GRU; skill falls from 0.379 to 0.239 and from 0.396 to 0.224. Quiet hours lose 19.8% and 25.1%, storm hours 56.1% and 68.9%. Every interval excludes zero except intense hours for XGBoost.",
  "Most of that loss is gaps, not noise: 18.6% of IMF hours and 27.0% of plasma hours are missing in the archive (daily tracking gaps, mostly 23 to 06 UT). On the 9,681 issue hours with every input observed over the last 6 hours the loss is 7.0% (XGBoost, interval touches zero) and 7.3% (GRU); only 31 storm hours are in that subset.",
  "The 1 hour delay is the right alignment (Bz correlation with OMNI 0.81 against 0.58 at 0 hours and 0.63 at 2 hours); with no delay the loss is 38% for both models.",
  "Real-time density is 2.75 per cc lower than OMNI on average (OMNI mean 6.58) and lower in 91% of hours, so pressure is 0.60 nPa low. The ACE Bt is the magnitude of the averaged vector: 0.53 nT below OMNI b_mag_avg but unbiased against OMNI b_vector_mag.",
  "Caveat: the live forecast reads the SWPC propagated product (mostly DSCOVR), whose coverage is far better than ACE real-time tracking in 2017 to 2020, so the all hours loss overstates the live gap; the inputs observed rows are the closer proxy."
 ],
